<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The phone line's FALLBACK answer, served by nginx on the public VPS.

  Twilio fetches this when the normal voice webhook fails or times out — the
  bridge machine is off, the SSH tunnel is down, the house has no power. Without
  it the caller hears Twilio's own "an application error has occurred" and the
  call ends; with it they hear one sentence and are put through to a person.

  It lives on the VPS ON PURPOSE. A fallback served by the machine that just
  died is not a fallback.

  GENERATED FILE. Do not edit it on the server. It is rendered per number by
  the render mode of plugins/phone_agent/twilio_config.py, from this template
  plus that business's name and forward number, into deploy/phone/rendered/.
  To change what a caller hears, edit the business's profile (or this
  template) and render it again.
-->
<Response>
  <Say>{{SAY}}</Say>
  {{ACTION}}
</Response>
